27, 2024</span></div><div class=\"mt-3 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-1.5\"><span class=\"text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-muted-foreground\">Topics<!-- -->:</span><span class=\"rounded-md border border-fuchsia-500/30 bg-fuchsia-600/5 px-2 py-0.5 text-xs text-fuchsia-700 dark:text-fuchsia-300\">#<!-- -->Smart City</span><span class=\"rounded-md border border-fuchsia-500/30 bg-fuchsia-600/5 px-2 py-0.5 text-xs text-fuchsia-700 dark:text-fuchsia-300\">#<!-- -->Startup</span><span class=\"rounded-md border border-fuchsia-500/30 bg-fuchsia-600/5 px-2 py-0.5 text-xs text-fuchsia-700 dark:text-fuchsia-300\">#<!-- -->IoT</span><span class=\"rounded-md border border-fuchsia-500/30 bg-fuchsia-600/5 px-2 py-0.5 text-xs text-fuchsia-700 dark:text-fuchsia-300\">#<!-- -->Traffic Management</span></div><h1 class=\"mt-4 text-3xl font-extrabold leading-tight sm:text-4xl\">What is a Smart City? (Smart City) Smart City Startup (Startup) - Smart City Projects Around the World</h1><div class=\"relative mt-7 aspect-[16/9] w-full overflow-hidden rounded-2xl shadow-lg\"><img alt=\"What is a Smart City? (Smart City) Smart City Startup (Startup) - Smart City Projects Around the World\" decoding=\"async\" data-nimg=\"fill\" class=\"object-cover\" style=\"position:absolute;height:100%;width:100%;left:0;top:0;right:0;bottom:0;color:transparent\" sizes=\"(min-width: 1024px) 768px, 100vw\" srcSet=\"/_next/image?url=%2Fmedia%2Foutput_13.webp&amp;w=640&amp;q=75 640w, /_next/image?url=%2Fmedia%2Foutput_13.webp&amp;w=750&amp;q=75 750w, /_next/image?url=%2Fmedia%2Foutput_13.webp&amp;w=828&amp;q=75 828w, /_next/image?url=%2Fmedia%2Foutput_13.webp&amp;w=1080&amp;q=75 1080w, /_next/image?url=%2Fmedia%2Foutput_13.webp&amp;w=1200&amp;q=75 1200w, /_next/image?url=%2Fmedia%2Foutput_13.webp&amp;w=1920&amp;q=75 1920w, /_next/image?url=%2Fmedia%2Foutput_13.webp&amp;w=2048&amp;q=75 2048w, /_next/image?url=%2Fmedia%2Foutput_13.webp&amp;w=3840&amp;q=75 3840w\" src=\"/_next/image?url=%2Fmedia%2Foutput_13.webp&amp;w=3840&amp;q=75\"/></div><div class=\"prose-blog mt-8\" dir=\"ltr\"><h1>Here we want to discuss what a Smart City is, Smart City startups, Smart City projects around the world, and also talk about the startup we have defined for Smart City. Join us</h1>\n\n<h2>What is a Smart City?</h2>\n\n\n\n\n\n<h4> “Smart City” means a city that uses smart technologies and solutions to improve the quality of life for its residents and manage urban issues. Among the technologies used in a Smart City are the Internet of Things, sensor networks, artificial intelligence and data analysis, fast and simple communication with citizens, traffic monitoring and control, urban safety and health, as well as reducing energy consumption and air pollution. The goal of a Smart City is to provide better services, optimize urban resources, and create a more comfortable life for residents</h4>\nsrc=\"/media/output_13ey.webp\"smart city – world<br />mehrdad startup 🌏\n\n<h3>What are the Smart City projects in the world?</h3>\n\n\n\n<h4>Smart City projects around the world are constantly expanding due to their special importance for improving the quality of life for residents and better managing cities. Below are a few examples of Smart City projects in the world:</h4>\n<ol>\n<li>\n<h4>Smart City Tokyo, Japan: This smart city uses technologies such as sensor networks, artificial intelligence and data analysis to manage traffic, energy consumption, waste, and health.</h4>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>Smart City Copenhagen, Denmark: This city uses an internet-connected system to manage traffic, street lighting, and safety.</h4>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>Smart City Barcelona, Spain: This city uses a smart system to manage buses, public institutions, street lighting, and traffic.</h4>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>Smart City Singapore: This city uses technologies such as the Internet of Things, artificial intelligence and data analysis to manage traffic, safety, security, and health.</h4>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>Smart City Los Angeles, United States: This city uses sensor networks, traffic monitoring and control, and parking management.</h4>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>Smart City Zurich, Switzerland: This city uses technologies such as the Internet of Things, sensor networks and data analysis to manage public transportation systems, reduce energy consumption, and optimize water usage.</h4>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>Smart City Hamburg, Germany: This city uses technologies such as the Internet of Things, sensor networks, artificial intelligence and data analysis to manage traffic, parking, safety, and security.</h4>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>Smart City Dubai, United Arab Emirates: This city uses technologies such as artificial intelligence, the Internet of Things and data analysis to manage traffic, safety, security, and health.</h4>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>Smart City Shanghai, China: This city uses technologies such as sensor networks, artificial intelligence, data analysis, and fast communication with citizens to manage traffic, security, health, and energy consumption.</h4>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<h3>These projects are just small examples of Smart City projects in the world, and new projects are being created around the world every day. The goal of these projects is to improve the quality of life for residents and better manage cities.</h3>\n<h2>Smart Cities in Saudi Arabia</h2>\n<h4>Saudi Arabia also uses Smart City projects to improve urban conditions. Currently, several Smart City projects in Saudi Arabia are being implemented and developed. For example:</h4>\n<ol>\n<li>\n<h4>Smart City Najran: This project includes installing smart sensors to collect data related to traffic, energy, environment, and health.</h4>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>Smart City Mecca: This project includes creating a smart management system to facilitate the reception of pilgrims at the Grand Mosque.</h4>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>Smart City Jeddah: This project includes creating a smart traffic management system and information centers for citizens.</h4>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>Smart City Riyadh: This project includes using communication technologies to manage traffic, parking, civic services, and provide services to travelers</h4>\n</li>\n</ol>\nsrc=\"/media/output_1sdg.webp\"مehrdad Smart city startup\n<h3>5-  Smart City alnama  in Saudi Arabia</h3>\n\n\n\n<h4>The Smart City “Alnama” in Saudi Arabia is one of the major and important projects in the field of Smart Cities in the world, created with the aim of improving living conditions for citizens and increasing economic efficiency. This city, located near the city of Mecca, uses advanced technologies such as the Internet of Things, machine learning, data analytics, and communication systems to implement the project.</h4>\n<h4>Alnama is divided into several sections, each designed with the goal of increasing efficiency and productivity in their respective sectors. Some of these sections include:</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<h4>Transportation sector: This sector includes roads, train lines, and airports that use new technologies to improve traffic conditions, reduce travel time, and provide better <a href=\"https://mehrdad.ir/%d8%b7%d8%b1%d8%a7%d8%ad%db%8c-%d8%b3%db%8c%d8%b3%d8%aa%d9%85-%d8%ad%d8%a7%d9%85%d9%84-%d9%88-%d9%86%d9%82%d9%84-%d9%86%d9%88%db%8c%d9%86/\" rel=\"noopener\">transportation</a>.</h4>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>Residential sector: This sector includes residential units that use smart technologies to provide convenience and security facilities for their residents.</h4>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>Administrative sector: This sector includes offices, hospitals, and universities that use smart technologies to provide better facilities for communication, security, and organization.</h4>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>The cost of this project is not currently precisely known, but various analyses indicate that its cost is in the billions of dollars. This project has received strong financial support from the Saudi Arabian government. For example, in 2018, the company “Nemat Al-Khair,” one of the companies constructing this project, announced that a contract worth $4.4 billion had been allocated to it for constructing the housing sector of Alnama. Also in 2019, the company “Apple” signed a contract worth $122 million with the company “Nemat Al-Khair” to provide smart technologies for Alnama.</h4>\n<h4>The Alnama project continues to progress steadily, and in 2021, companies “Microsoft” and “Apple” also announced that they had signed contracts to provide technical and research services in various fields including <a href=\"https://mehrdad.ir/%d8%a7%db%8c%d9%86%d8%aa%d8%b1%d9%86%d8%aa-%d8%a7%d8%b4%db%8c%d8%a7-iot-internet-of-things-%da%86%db%8c%d8%b3%d8%aa-%d8%9f/\" rel=\"noopener\">Internet of Things</a> and urban data analytics in Alnama. Additionally, to implement this project, other companies such as “Cisco,” “IBM,” and “Intel” have also signed contracts to provide technical and research services in Alnama.</h4><h4>Technologies used in this <a href=\"https://mehrdad.ir/%d9%81%d8%b1%d8%b5%d8%aa-%d9%87%d8%a7%db%8c-%d8%b3%d8%b1%d9%85%d8%a7%db%8c%d9%87-%da%af%d8%b0%d8%a7%d8%b1%db%8c-%d9%86%d8%b1%d9%85-%d8%a7%d9%81%d8%b2%d8%a7%d8%b1-%d9%87%d8%a7%db%8c-%d9%85%d8%a7/\" rel=\"noopener\">project</a> include the Internet of Things, data analytics, intelligent lighting, heating, and cooling systems, and communication systems. Overall, Neom Smart City is recognized as one of the largest and most advanced smart city projects in the world, implemented with the goal of improving the quality of life for Neom citizens and reducing operational and environmental costs. This project is not only considered a prime example of a smart city but also a prominent technological project globally.</h4>\n\n<h4>Currently, Neom is still expanding, and there are plans for its improvement and expansion in the future. For example, in 2021, the company \"Nemah Al-Khair\" announced that it had signed a $55 million contract to provide technical and research services for Neom. Additionally, there are plans in this project to use new technologies such as artificial intelligence, robotics, and virtual reality.</h4>\n<h4>In general, Neom Smart City is a prime example of smart city projects in the world, which has helped improve the quality of life for citizens and reduce operational and environmental costs in this city by using modern technologies and smart management.</h4>\n<h4>The companies responsible for implementing the Neom Smart City project are the Saudi companies \"Nishan\" and \"Al-Riyadh.\" Additionally, a large number of technology companies and consultants have been used for this project.</h4>\n<h4>The area of Neom city is approximately 32,500 hectares. To implement the smart city project, a large number of workers, employees, and engineers were at work. Overall, this project has created jobs for more than 10,000 people.</h4>\n<h4>Currently, more than 90% of the Neom Smart City project has been completed. Improvements are still being made in various urban areas. Overall, this is a long-term project that will continue until its initial goals are achieved.</h4>\n<p> </p>\n<h3>The main goal of the Neom Smart City project is to create a smart and sustainable city using new and innovative technologies. This project, by using smart systems in various fields such as energy, transportation, waste management, and water, strives to improve citizens' quality of life, reduce costs, and improve efficiency in resource utilization. Additionally, another goal of this project is to create an information and communication technology center in the Middle East region.</h3>\n\n<h2>In the fields of energy, transportation, waste management, and water, Neom Smart City has used various technologies. Below, we highlight some of the activities of this smart city in each of these areas:</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<h4>Energy: In the energy sector, Neom Smart City uses wind turbines, solar panels, smart energy management systems, and battery storage. The main goal of these activities is to reduce energy consumption, improve efficiency, and reduce greenhouse gas emissions.</h4>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>Transportation: In the transportation sector, Neom Smart City uses smart, autonomous, and electric vehicles. Additionally, this smart city uses smart traffic and parking systems, which lead to improved urban traffic and reduced travel time for citizens.</h4>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>Waste Management: In the waste management sector, Neom Smart City uses smart systems for collecting, separating, and recycling waste. These systems operate automatically using sensors and IoT networks, leading to reduced waste collection and recycling costs.</h4>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>Water: In the water sector, Neom Smart City uses smart water consumption control systems and smart water management systems. These systems lead to reduced water consumption.</h4>\n</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h4>In the transportation sector, Neom Smart City has an advanced public transportation system that includes electric buses and driverless taxis. This smart city currently has a dedicated system for monitoring and managing traffic, which uses smart technologies such as sensors, cameras, data collection equipment, and intelligent algorithms. This system has improved traffic and reduced travel time in the city.</h4>\n<h4>In the waste management sector, Neom Smart City uses smart waste management systems that include automated waste collection devices and CCTV systems for monitoring the waste collection and disposal process. Additionally, advanced technologies are used in this smart city to recover reusable materials from waste and reduce its production.</h4>\n<h4>In the water resource management sector, Neom Smart City uses new water management systems. For example, this smart city has a smart system to control water consumption in its green spaces and smart homes. Additionally, water collection and recycling systems are used for irrigation in green spaces and car washing.</h4>\n<h4>Among other innovations of this smart city is the use of technology in the field of</h4>\n<h4>waste management, Neom Smart City uses a smart system that, by using sensor systems, collection equipment, data processing, and artificial intelligence, performs waste management in the most optimal way possible. Some of the actions taken in this area include:</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<h4>Use of sensor systems: In Neom Smart City, sensor systems are used to detect the fill level of waste bins and collect information related to waste.</h4>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>Collection equipment: Neom Smart City uses advanced collection equipment for waste collection. This equipment includes high-intelligence collection trucks and waste containers.</h4>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>Data processing and artificial intelligence: Data collected by sensor systems is processed using artificial intelligence algorithms. Using these algorithms, the optimal waste collection route, the optimal time for waste collection, and other factors are calculated.</h4>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>In the water management sector as well, Neom Smart City uses a smart system that, by using sensor systems, collection equipment, and data processing, performs water management in the most optimal way possible.</h4>\n<h4>Neom Smart City, as one of the largest smart city construction and development projects in the world, considering the needs and priorities of its citizens, strives to make citizens' lives easier and better using modern technologies and to transform the city into a sustainable one.</h4>\n<h4>The goals of Neom Smart City include:</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<h4>Reducing energy costs and optimizing energy consumption in buildings</h4>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>Optimizing public transportation and increasing ease of use for citizens</h4>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>Reducing traffic and increasing driver and pedestrian safety</h4>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>Improving waste management and recycling of reusable materials</h4>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>Optimizing water consumption and improving the quality of urban water</h4>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>Enhancing urban security and reducing the crime rate in the city</h4>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>Increasing communication between citizens and providing electronic services in an easy and quick manner.</h4>\n</li>\n</ul><h4>Since the smart city of Alnama is still under construction and development, its goals and objectives may change over time and evolve to align with new needs and urban conditions</h4>\n<p> </p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<h3>In the next post, we will explain the startup we have designed for the smart city</h3>\n\n<h5>Thank you Mehrdad</h5>\n\n<p dir=\"ltr\">Short Link:<br />\n<a href=\"https://mehrdad.ir/b7if\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>https://mehrdad.ir/b7if</strong></a></p></div><aside aria-label=\"Ready to turn this into a product?\" class=\"mt-10 rounded-2xl border border-violet-500/30 bg-gradient-to-br from-violet-600/10 to-fuchsia-600/10 p-5 sm:p-6\"><h2 class=\"flex items-center gap-2 text-lg font-bold leading-snug\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-rocket h-5 w-5 shrink-0 text-violet-500\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M4.5 16.5c-1.5 1.26-2 5-2 5s3.74-.5 5-2c.71-.84.7-2.13-.09-2.91a2.18 2.18 0 0 0-2.91-.09z\"></path><path d=\"m12 15-3-3a22 22 0 0 1 2-3.95A12.88 12.88 0 0 1 22 2c0 2.72-.78 7.5-6 11a22.35 22.35 0 0 1-4 2z\"></path><path d=\"M9 12H4s.55-3.03 2-4c1.62-1.08 5 0 5 0\"></path><path d=\"M12 15v5s3.03-.55 4-2c1.08-1.62 0-5 0-5\"></path></svg>Ready to turn this into a product?</h2><p class=\"mt-1.5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground\">In one AI MVP Sprint I take your idea from first sketch to a live product — in weeks, not months.</p><div class=\"mt-4 flex flex-col gap-2.5 sm:flex-row sm:items-center\"><a class=\"inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 rounded-xl bg-gradient-to-r from-violet-600 to-fuchsia-6